          <h2 id="when-not">When a Wheel Is the Wrong Tool</h2>
          <p>
            A wheel is a convenience for low-stakes choices among acceptable
            options, and it is worth being honest about where it does not
            belong.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>High-stakes decisions.</strong> Medical, legal,
              financial and career choices need information and judgment, not
              chance.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Options that are not equally acceptable.</strong> If one
              entry is clearly better, pick it. A wheel only helps when you are
              genuinely indifferent.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Safety and fairness checks.</strong> Where a result
              affects other people's opportunities, such as prizes or grades,
              decide the rules openly first. Our guides on
              <a href="/blogs/how-to-run-online-giveaway">running an online giveaway</a>
              and
              <a href="/blogs/school-raffle-spin-wheel">school raffles</a>
              cover transparent setups.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Curious about the alternatives? We compare them in
